(\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\cos 4t, 0,-\\sin 4t⟩)/((\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}})) \\\\\n&= ⟨\\cos 4t, 0,-\\sin 4t⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the binormal vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nB(t) &= T(t) \\cdot N(t) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\sin 4t, 2, \\cos 4t⟩ \\cdot ⟨\\cos 4t, 0,-\\sin 4t⟩ \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}i\\begin{vmatrix}j & k \\\\ \\sin 4t & 2\\end{vmatrix}\\cos 4t \\\\\n&= \\cos 4t \\mid 0\\begin{vmatrix}-\\sin 4t \\\\ = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[2\\begin{vmatrix}\\cos 4t \\\\ 0\\end{vmatrix}- \\sin 4ti - \\sin 4t\\begin{vmatrix}\\cos 4t \\\\ \\cos 4t\\end{vmatrix}- \\sin 4tj + \\sin 4t \\mid 2 \\\\\n&= \\cos 4t\\end{vmatrix}0k] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨ - 2\\sin 4t - 0, - (-\\sin^{2} 4t - \\cos^{2} 4t), 0 - 2\\cos 4t⟩ \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨ - 2\\sin 4t, 1,-2\\cos 4t⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535879 false] [17592186166611 1145 "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf B(t) = \\mathbf T(t) \\times \\mathbf N(t),\n$$\n\nwhere the principal normal vector $\\mathbf N(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf N(t)= \\dfrac{\\mathbf T'(t)}{\\|\\mathbf T'(t)\\|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal normal $\\mathbf{N}(t).$ To do this, we calculate $\\mathbf T'(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,0,\\,-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{16{cos}^{2}⁡4t+16{sin}^{2}⁡4t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{16({cos}^{2}⁡4t+{sin}^{2}⁡4t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize $\\mathbf T'(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t⟩}{(\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}})} \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the binormal vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t,2,\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t⟩\\times ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡4t & 2 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t & 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t & 2 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t-0,-(-{sin}^{2}⁡4t-{cos}^{2}⁡4t),0-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t,\\,1,\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535879 true] [17592186166767 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372007 13194139535879 true] [17592186166767 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372014 13194139535879 true] [17592186166767 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372028 13194139535879 true] [17592186166767 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372035 13194139535879 true] [17592186166768 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372042 13194139535879 true] [17592186166768 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372049 13194139535879 true] [17592186166768 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372056 13194139535879 true] [17592186166768 1020 #edb/ref 17592186372063 13194139535879 true] [17592186166769 1020 #edb/ref 175